{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>But you, not so.</b> That is: and you, who are the portion of HaShem — HaShem your Elohim has not given you to hearken to the diviners and the soothsayers and to seek them, for He will establish for you prophets, and you will know future things from the side of prophecy. This is what it says: 'a prophet from your midst, from your brethren.'" "<b>Behold.</b> This is a great superiority: there is no true knowledge of the future that will never prove false except from the side of prophecy, for all other future-knowledge is doubtful. Therefore prophecy was compared to winnowed grain separated from the straw, as it is written (Jeremiah 23:28): ״מה לתבן את הבר נאם ה׳ צבאות״, and the prophecy of false prophets is compared to straw, because in a minority of cases they are right — just as in straw there are sometimes a few grains of wheat; but prophecy is certain, entirely truth, with no admixture at all, in the manner of grain in which no straw is found at all but is cleared from it — which is why Scripture used the term בר (winnowed grain) and not דגן or חטה. And because the Holy One, blessed be He, acted wondrously in the creation of His world upon three divisions — the lower, the intermediate, and the upper — and created man composed as a composite of all of them, He wished to place in his hand wisdom to know future things from all the divisions: from the lower world, which is the world of the elements — birds and demons, from which man knows future things; from the intermediate world, which is the clairvoyants; from the upper world, the prophets — for the prophecy of every prophet besides Moses is only through an angel. The future-knowledge of the clairvoyant is doubtful, as the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded (Isaiah 47:13): ״מאשר יבאו עליך״ — 'what comes upon you' (מאשר), and not 'all that comes' (כל אשר) — and needless to say the future-knowledge of the bird and the demon. But the future-knowledge of the prophet is certain; it is the greatest superiority of all the divisions. And since you will have prophets, you have no need to seek unto the dead on behalf of the living." "<b>And know</b> that these three divisions, each one of them receives substitution from the division that is above it, for the power of the upper has the ability to exchange the action of the lower. For the lower world receives substitution from the power of the intermediate world, and likewise the intermediate world receives substitution from the power of the upper world, and likewise the upper from the power of the Supreme One, blessed be He, who is supreme over all. And the allusion to this is (Genesis 28:13): ״והנה ה׳ נצב עליו״ — upon these three divisions, which He encompassed under the name 'ladder.' And you shall understand from this that the bird and the demon are falsehood compared to the clairvoyant, and likewise the clairvoyant is falsehood compared to the prophet, and the prophet compared to the Supreme One, blessed be He — and this is in the matter of evil, as we find with Hezekiah and Jonah, but not in the matter of good."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:22.026212395Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}